#### Step-by-Step Explanation

The problem involves calculating how long it will take to install the remaining windows of a new building.

1. **Total windows required**: 14  
2. **Windows already installed**: 8  
3. **Remaining windows**:  
   $$
   \text{Remaining windows} = \text{Total windows} - \text{Installed windows} = 14 - 8 = 6
   $$
4. **Time to install one window**: 8 hours  
5. **Total time to install remaining windows**:  
   $$
   \text{Total time} = \text{Number of remaining windows} \times \text{Time per window} = 6 \times 8 = 48
   $$

