  3 \text{ shelves} \times 4 \text{ books/shelf} = 12 \text{ books}
  $$

Adding these two quantities together gives the total number of books:  
$$
20 \text{ books} + 12 \text{ books} = 32 \text{ books}
$$

Alternatively, since there are a total of $ 5 + 3 = 8 $ shelves and each shelf has 4 books, we can also calculate the total as:  
$$
