Megan baked 71 cupcakes. Her brother, Todd, took 43 of them. To find out how many cupcakes Megan has left, we subtract 43 from 71:

$$
71 - 43 = 28
$$

Next, we need to determine how many packages of 7 cupcakes each can be made from the remaining 28 cupcakes. We divide 28 by 7:

$$
28 \div 7 = 4
$$

Thus, Megan can make $\boxed{4}$ packages. 
