The problem involves determining how many students are in each group after some have been excluded and the rest divided equally. 

First, there are 65 students trying out. Out of these, 17 did not get picked for the team. To find the number of students who were picked, we subtract the number of students not picked from the total number of students:

$$
65 - 17 = 48
$$

So, 48 students were selected to be on the team. These 48 students are then divided equally into 8 groups. To find out how many students are in each group, we divide the number of selected students by the number of groups:

$$
48 \div 8 = 6
$$

Thus, each group has $\boxed{6}$ students. 

