Kaeb starts with 12 dollars. He spends 8 dollars on a new game, so he has $12 - 8 = 4$ dollars left. Each toy costs 2 dollars. To find out how many toys he can buy with the remaining 4 dollars, we divide:

$$
\frac{4}{2} = 2
$$

Therefore, Kaeb can buy $\boxed{2}$ toys. This is also confirmed by the fact that buying 2 toys would cost $2 \times 2 = 4$ dollars, which matches the remaining amount he has. No additional toys can be purchased as that would require 6 dollars, which he does not have. 

