Initially, there are 46 books. A librarian takes 10 of them, leaving Oliver with:

$$
46 - 10 = 36 \text{ books}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate how many shelves are needed

Each shelf holds 4 books. To find how many shelves are required, divide the number of books by the capacity of each shelf:

$$
36 \div 4 = 9
$$

Since this division results in an exact integer and no remainder, Oliver can perfectly fit all 36 books on 9 shelves. There is no need for an additional shelf.

---

