Lukr has 5 piles of quarters and 5 piles of dimes. Each pile contains 3 coins. 

First, calculate the total number of coins in the quarters:  
$$ 5 \text{ piles} \times 3 \text{ coins per pile} = 15 \text{ coins} $$

Next, calculate the total number of coins in the dimes:  
$$ 5 \text{ piles} \times 3 \text{ coins per pile} = 15 \text{ coins} $$

Add the two amounts together to find the total number of coins:  
$$ 15 \text{ coins (quarters)} + 15 \text{ coins (dimes)} = 30 \text{ coins} $$

Alternatively, you can calculate the total number of piles (5 quarters + 5 dimes = 10 piles) and multiply by the number of coins per pile:  
$$ 10 \text{ piles} \times 3 \text{ coins per pile} = 30 \text{ coins} $$

Therefore, the total number of coins Lukr has is $\boxed{30}$.  
